  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In interhalogen compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AB</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;Central atom A is halogen so it contain <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> electrons in its outer most shell. so its structure is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/40210c6f-7231-4c17-8377-6895a8e881c5-image.png\" style=\"width: 199px; height: 156px;\" /></p><p>So central atom A contain <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> lone pairs of electrons.</p>",
